>(1) What exactly do loadstones do and why is everyone always so happy
>to get them or maybe its luckstones or whatever. In any case, what's the
>deal with those stones?

	Luck is one of the stats the game tracks without you being able to see
it.  Ordinarily, your luck is adjusted towards 0 every few hundred turns.  A
normal luckstone adds three points to your luck (max of 10 or 11) and sustains
it at that level.  A blessed luckstone also adds three points, but only
sustains positive luck.  A cursed stone subtracts three points and sustains
negative luck.

>(2) How many different types of spped are there? ...

	Two.  Intrinsic speed, which can be gotten innumerable ways, gives you
an extra move every few turns.  Speed bestowed by speed boots, potions, or the
spell Haste Self gives you an extra move every turn.

>(3) If I convert an altar inside a temple with a priest, and the priest
>attacks me, is there any way I can avoid losing my ESP?

	Well, you will lose intrinsic ESP if you kill the priest, so if you
can get rid of the priest without killing him, you'll be ok.  You'd best
consider this before converting the altar.

>(4) How can I protect myself so that Liches Nagas and Titans can't make
>my items vanish? It's very annoying, specially when they're blessed
>rustproof +2 gauntlets of power

	You need some form of magic resistance.  Magic resistance can be had
via a cloak of m.r., a suit of gray dragon scale mail, or the Knight's Quest
item (the Magic Mirror of Merlin, I think.)  That will make you immune to a
lot of magical attacks, including the dreaded 'touch of death,' but it won't
keep them from cursing your stuff.

